WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.650
So Chapter 04 adds a tool:
workflow payload dot p y.

2
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:07.304
It picks the workflow
for the trigger you name,

3
00:00:07.304 --> 00:00:11.075
and resolves the body's dollar keys
against a saved trigger input.

4
00:00:11.075 --> 00:00:14.825
It handles simple paths only,
like dollar dot a dot b.

5
00:00:14.825 --> 00:00:20.312
Anything more complex is refused,
because the tool isn't a JSONPath engine.

6
00:00:20.312 --> 00:00:24.892
Then it derives the intended state
exactly as the ServiceNow script does,

7
00:00:24.892 --> 00:00:27.821
checks the payload against
Module 1's contract,

8
00:00:27.821 --> 00:00:31.425
and lists the input's top-level
fields the body doesn't send.

9
00:00:31.425 --> 00:00:33.688
That last line is where gaps show up.

10
00:00:33.688 --> 00:00:38.440
Three fictional trigger inputs come with
it: a native change to Alice's account, a

11
00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.671
department change on Erin's identity,

12
00:00:40.671 --> 00:00:43.551
and a successful provisioning
action for Alice.

13
00:00:43.551 --> 00:00:46.935
One caution: the tool shows
what the body says to send,

14
00:00:46.935 --> 00:00:49.612
not what SailPoint's step actually sends.

15
00:00:49.612 --> 00:00:51.740
Lab 2 settles that for your tenant.
